\subsection*{1.4 Composition of Functions and Invertible Function}

Definition 8 Let \(f: \mathrm{A} \rightarrow \mathrm{B}\) and \(g: \mathrm{B} \rightarrow \mathrm{C}\) be two functions. Then the composition of \(f\) and \(g\), denoted by gof, is defined as the function \(g o f: \mathrm{A} \rightarrow \mathrm{C}\) given by
\[g o f(x)=g(f(x)), \forall x \in \mathrm{~A} .\]

