Example 18 If \(\mathrm{A}=\left[\begin{array}{rrr}1 & 2 & 3 \\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\ 4 & 2 & 1\end{array}\right]\), then show that \(\mathrm{A}^{3}-23 \mathrm{~A}-40 \mathrm{I}=\mathrm{O}\)

