17. Let \(\vec{a}\) and \(\vec{b}\) be two unit vectors and \(\theta\) is the angle between them. Then \(\vec{a}+\vec{b}\) is a unit vector if
(A) \(\theta=\frac{\pi}{4}\)
(B) \(\theta=\frac{\pi}{3}\)
